course: dictionary
lesson: 9174
title: Snug: warm, safe and close-fitting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Snug has two meanings. The first is warm, comfortable and safe, like a child «snug in bed». The second is fitting closely, with no extra space, like «a snug fit». Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: Look for clues. «A helmet fits snug and level, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled; a loose helmet does not protect.» Here snug is about fit. The word loose is the clue: it is the opposite of snug, so snug must mean fitting closely.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: «a helmet fits close and level, with the strap buckled» still makes sense, so snug means fitting closely here. Try the same check on «snug in bed»: warm and comfortable still makes sense.
fact: Snug means warm, comfortable and safe, as in «snug in bed».
fact: Snug also means fitting closely, with no extra space, as in «a snug fit».
fact: «Snug as a bug in a rug» is a saying that means very warm and comfortable.
fact: Cosy is a similar word for the first meaning; Americans spell it «cozy».
fact: «A helmet protects only if it fits: snug, level on the head, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled.»
exercise: «The chin strap should be snug, with only a finger or two fitting under it.» What does snug mean here? | *Fitting closely, with no extra space | Warm and comfy in bed | Very old | Loud and noisy
exercise: «Mia was snug under her duvet, listening to the rain.» What does snug mean here? | Wet through | Very hungry | Fitting closely, with no extra space | *Warm, comfortable and safe
exercise: Which description shows a helmet that will protect you? | Loose and sliding around | Two sizes too big | Hanging off the handlebars | *Snug and level, with the strap buckled
test: «The lid is a snug fit on the jar.» What does snug mean? | *Fitting closely, with no extra space | Very fast | Loud and rude | Cold and wet
test: «The kitten curled up snug in its basket by the fire.» What does snug mean? | Cold and hungry | Very fast | Loud and rude | *Warm, comfortable and safe
exam: Which word means nearly the same as snug in «a snug fit»? | Hungry | *Tight | Loud | Wet
